        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(acp): close SQLite event ledger on shutdown to prevent file lock leaks",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `createSqliteAcpEventLedger` in `src/acp/event-ledger.ts` creates `DatabaseSync` connections that are never closed during ACP server shutdown / gateway hot reload. Old connections accumulate, leaking file descriptors and causing SQLite file lock contention.\n\nFixes #100637\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`src/acp/event-ledger.ts`** — Add `close()` method to `AcpEventLedger` interface; implement in `createSqliteAcpEventLedger` (close db + WAL maintenance) and `createLedgerApi` (no-op for in-memory)\n- **`src/acp/server.ts`** — Call `eventLedger.close()` during ACP server shutdown\n- **`src/acp/event-ledger.test.ts`** — Add test verifying close() releases the connection while preserving persisted state\n\n## Evidence\n\n```\npnpm exec vitest run src/acp/event-ledger.test.ts\n\n# In-memory tests: ✓ all pass\n# SQLite tests: ✓ persist state across ledger instances after close\n# New close test: ✓ releases connection, data survives reopen\n```\n\n## Related\n\n- Issue: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/100637\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
